Z||000000||Dan010||10-21-2001||09:43 PM||||Been reading everything, very interesting and helpful, I am interested in the engine swaps described here, all of them!<BR>Am now interest in what this would do to furture value of the Fiero as a collector<BR>car? I also realize that the value is to the behokder of the fine auto!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-21-2001||09:57 PM||||I'll say the same thing that Archie says on his website ( <A HREF="http://www.V8Archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.V8Archie.com</A>  ).  It depends on whom you're selling it to.  Some Fieroholics think that the only good Fiero is a 100% stock one and anything you do to one that isn't OEM is a crime.  There are others who would modify theirs forever and don't care about OEMness (I just made that up).  Most of us are somewhere in between.<P>I'd say the value of the car would increase with the value of the new engine.  If you spend $10k and have Archie install a brand new SBC, then I'd say your cars value will increase a few thousand bucks at least.  If you have the stock 2.8 rebuilt, your cars value will still go up (it has a new motor) but not as much.  Fieros aren't collectors cars.  They may never be.  (This has been debated here a number of times.)  If you want a car that's guaranteed to increase in value, pick something else.  If you want something that's unique and fun to drive, keep your Fiero.<P>Welcome to the forum.||||reg||1
